  {
    "_comment": "VOICE FAMILIES. A creature.json says \"voice\": \"beast\" and every voiced sound",
    "_comment2": "it makes looks for beast_<id> before falling back to the plain one above. Four",
    "_comment3": "families and four sounds each is enough to make a roster sound like it has",
    "_comment4": "characters in it; unwritten ids simply fall through, so a family is never",
    "_comment5": "obliged to cover everything. Each is still pitched per creature, which is why",
    "_comment6": "one family does not turn into one voice shared by a dozen creatures.",
    "id": "_families"
  },

